[ti:Harbor Lights]
[ar:Wren & the Lowlands]
[al:Harbor Lights]
[au:W. Ashdown]
[by:MusicWave]
[length:03:01]
[re:MusicWave arrangement compiler]
[00:11.16]My father built a boat of pine
[00:16.74]he sanded every board by hand
[00:22.33]he said the sea will keep its time
[00:27.91]but you will always know the land
[00:33.49][01:18.14][02:25.12]So leave the harbor lights on
[00:39.07][01:23.72][02:30.70]leave them burning through the night
[00:44.65][01:29.30][02:36.28]no matter how far I've gone
[00:50.23][01:34.88][02:41.86]I'll be steering by your light
[00:55.81]I sailed beyond the northern bay
[01:01.40]where all the maps run out of names
[01:06.98]the stars were strangers on the way
[01:12.56]but every lighthouse looked the same
[02:02.79]Now my own hair is turning gray
[02:08.37]I sand the boards the way he showed
[02:13.95]and when you're ready, sail away
[02:19.53]I'll keep the light on down the road
[01:39.77]
[02:46.74]
